[PATCH] usb: kbd: Do not require an initial HID report during probe
USB HID 键盘初始化过程中存在不必要的强制报告读取，导致空闲状态下不主动发送 HID Report 的键盘被错误拒绝注册。
既然首次报告不是所有键盘都能提供的，为什么要把它作为通用的 probe 成功条件？
USB keyboard probing should not depend on receiving an initial HID input report.
**usb: kbd: Do not require an initial HID report during probe**

The USB keyboard driver currently performs a synchronous Interrupt IN transfer during probing and rejects the keyboard if the transfer fails.

However, an idle keyboard may not immediately return an input report. Some keyboards only generate reports when their key state changes, even after a successful SET_IDLE request.

As a result, a fully enumerated and otherwise functional keyboard may be rejected simply because no key event occurred during the initial polling period.

This issue was observed with a USB keyboard (VID:PID 05af:0802) connected to the DWC3/XHCI controller on an RK3328 platform running U-Boot v2026.07.

The following behavior was observed:

- USB enumeration and endpoint configuration completed successfully.
- SET_PROTOCOL and SET_IDLE both returned success.
- The initial Interrupt IN transfer timed out with -ETIMEDOUT when no key was pressed.
- Pressing a key during initialization allowed the transfer to complete and the keyboard to initialize successfully.
- Changing the SET_IDLE duration did not resolve the issue.
- Skipping the initial report check using USB_HID_QUIRK_POLL_NO_REPORT_IDLE allowed the keyboard to be detected.

The existing quirks for Apple and Keychron keyboards already demonstrate that an initial input report is not a reliable prerequisite for keyboard detection.

Requiring this transfer for other keyboards can lead to false probe failures and unnecessary USB initialization delays.

Remove the mandatory initial input report check while preserving USB interface and endpoint validation.

This avoids rejecting otherwise functional keyboards solely because they do not produce an input report while idle, improving USB keyboard compatibility and probe robustness without requiring device-specific quirks.

Signed-off-by: liu shiwei <liushiwei@gmail.com>


diff -uNra b/common/usb_kbd.c c/common/usb_kbd.c
--- b/common/usb_kbd.c	2026-07-07 07:50:43.000000000 +0800
+++ c/common/usb_kbd.c	2026-10-18 11:49:59.315612533 +0800
@@ -33,8 +33,6 @@
 
 #define USB_VENDOR_ID_KEYCHRON	0x3434
 
-#define USB_HID_QUIRK_POLL_NO_REPORT_IDLE	BIT(0)
-
 /*
  * If overwrite_console returns 1, the stdin, stderr and stdout
  * are switched to the serial port, else the settings in the
@@ -483,7 +481,6 @@
 	struct usb_interface *iface;
 	struct usb_endpoint_descriptor *ep;
 	struct usb_kbd_pdata *data;
-	unsigned int quirks = 0;
 	int epNum;
 
 	if (dev->descriptor.bNumConfigurations != 1)
@@ -516,15 +513,6 @@
 
 	debug("USB KBD: found interrupt EP: 0x%x\n", ep->bEndpointAddress);
 
-	switch (dev->descriptor.idVendor) {
-	case USB_VENDOR_ID_APPLE:
-	case USB_VENDOR_ID_KEYCHRON:
-		quirks |= USB_HID_QUIRK_POLL_NO_REPORT_IDLE;
-		break;
-	default:
-		break;
-	}
-
 	data = malloc(sizeof(struct usb_kbd_pdata));
 	if (!data) {
 		printf("USB KBD: Error allocating private data\n");
@@ -566,13 +554,12 @@
 #endif
 
 	/*
-	 * Apple and Keychron keyboards do not report the device state. Reports
+	 * Some keyboards do not report the device state. Reports
 	 * are only returned during key presses.
 	 */
-	if (quirks & USB_HID_QUIRK_POLL_NO_REPORT_IDLE) {
-		debug("USB KBD: quirk: skip testing device state\n");
-		return 1;
-	}
+#ifdef CONFIG_SYS_USB_EVENT_POLL
+	debug("USB KBD: skip testing device state\n");
+#else
 	debug("USB KBD: enable interrupt pipe...\n");
 #ifdef CONFIG_SYS_USB_EVENT_POLL_VIA_INT_QUEUE
 	data->intq = create_int_queue(dev, data->intpipe, 1,
@@ -582,16 +569,13 @@
 #elif defined(CONFIG_SYS_USB_EVENT_POLL_VIA_CONTROL_EP)
 	if (usb_get_report(dev, iface->desc.bInterfaceNumber,
 			   1, 0, data->new, USB_KBD_BOOT_REPORT_SIZE) < 0) {
-#else
-	if (usb_int_msg(dev, data->intpipe, data->new, data->intpktsize,
-			data->intinterval, false) < 0) {
 #endif
 		printf("Failed to get keyboard state from device %04x:%04x\n",
 		       dev->descriptor.idVendor, dev->descriptor.idProduct);
 		/* Abort, we don't want to use that non-functional keyboard. */
 		return 0;
 	}
-
+#endif
 	/* Success. */
 	return 1;
 }
